2. NATURE OF THE SOFTWARE — READ THIS BEFORE USE
================================================================================

The Software is NETWORKING SOFTWARE. It creates encrypted virtual private
networks between computers, and in doing so it:

  * installs and operates a VIRTUAL NETWORK ADAPTER on the host system, which
    requires ADMINISTRATOR / ELEVATED PRIVILEGES;
  * performs NAT TRAVERSAL ("hole punching"), which deliberately opens paths
    through network address translators and may bypass assumptions made by
    firewalls and other network controls;
  * ENCRYPTS traffic between peers, rendering that traffic opaque to network
    operators, security monitoring and inspection systems;
  * CARRIES ARBITRARY IP TRAFFIC, including broadcast and multicast, between
    connected machines, causing remote machines to appear as though they are on
    your local network.

CONSEQUENTLY, MISCONFIGURATION OR MISUSE OF THE SOFTWARE CAN CREATE SERIOUS
SECURITY RISKS — NOT ONLY FOR YOU, BUT FOR THIRD PARTIES, FOR THE NETWORKS YOU
CONNECT TO, AND FOR ANYONE WHOSE SYSTEMS BECOME REACHABLE THROUGH A TUNNEL YOU
ESTABLISH. Connecting a machine to a peer effectively extends a network
boundary. You are responsible for understanding that consequence before you
use the Software.

